# GC Career Studio — environment variable reference
#
# Set up:  copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
#          `.env` is git-ignored; never commit a real `.env`.
#
# On Vercel, the Prisma Postgres integration injects DATABASE_URL for you —
# you do NOT set it in the Vercel dashboard. Set it in your LOCAL `.env`
# only so `npx prisma db push` / `npm run db:seed` can target the hosted
# database from this machine.

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL use only (Vercel injects its own):
#   Paste the DIRECT, non-pooled connection string from
#   Vercel → Storage → your Prisma Postgres database → "Get connection strings"
#   (host `db.prisma.io`, contains `?sslmode=require`).
#   Use the NON-pooled URL for db push — pooled URLs reject DDL like CREATE TABLE.
#   An already-set OS environment variable named DATABASE_URL OVERRIDES this
#   file, so delete any stale one (e.g. an old Railway/Render host) first.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:secret@db.prisma.io:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# --- Auth.js -------------------------------------------------------------
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
# Exact public origin of the app — no trailing slash.
# Local:      http://localhost:3000
# On Vercel:  https://your-project.vercel.app
AUTH_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app

# --- Seed admin (consumed by prisma/seed.ts) ------------------------------
# The database is empty when first created. `npm run db:seed` creates the
# admin account + services + demo testimonials.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# Minimum 8 characters. Change this after first login.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-strong-password
ADMIN_NAME=GC Career Studio Admin

# --- Optional: Career Direction Assistant ----------------------------------
# The app runs fully without these; the feature degrades gracefully.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=